<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.4.4: Determining the Best Method for Solving a System of Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00419</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.4.4: Determining the Best Method for Solving a System of Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c0a92d35-0987-4d7f-953f-f33194a19303</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<para>Graphing technology should not be used in this cool down.
</para>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Use this linear equation to answer questions 1 - 2.</para>
<para> \(\left\{\begin{array}{c}2x+\frac12y=7\\6x- \frac12y=5\end{array}\right.\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which would be a more helpful method for solving the system? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Adding the two equations</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Explain or show how you know. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
<para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. \(\frac12y + − \frac12y = 0\), so adding the equations would eliminate the \(y\)-variable and enable solving for \(x\).</para>
<para>Solve the system without graphing to answer questions 3 – 5.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> Identify the \(x\) coordinate of the solution. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
<para>\(\frac32\) or equivalent</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> Identify the \(y\) coordinate of the solution. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 8</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> Explain or show your reasoning. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
<para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
<para> \(\begin{array}{r}\underline{\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;2x+\frac12y=7\\+\;\;\;\;\;\;6x-\frac12y=5}\\8x=12\\x=\frac{12}8\\x=\frac32\\\end{array}\) </para>

<para> \(\begin{array}{r}2x+\frac12y=7\\2(\frac32)+\frac12y=7\\3+\frac12y=7\\\frac12y=4\\y=8\\\end{array}\) </para>
<title>Video: Determining the Best Method for Solving a System of Equations</title>
<para> Watch the following video to learn more about finding the best method to solve a system of equations.</para>
